<!--
	The capital B of the mark.

	This outline is not hand drawn. It is the real glyph outline of a bold
	neo-grotesque capital B, the Helvetica family that Bloomberg's own mark is
	set in, taken directly from the font and mapped onto the 108 unit adaptive
	icon grid. Earlier revisions approximated the letter with rounded
	rectangles, which is why the bowls looked too circular and the whole thing
	read as geometric rather than grotesque.

	Geometry notes, in grid units:
	  cap height 52, from y=28 to y=80, so the letter is centred vertically
	  ink width 43.56, centred at x=32.22
	  half diagonal of the ink box 33.92, inside the 36 radius circle that the
	  circular launcher mask leaves visible, so no corner of the letter can be
	  clipped on any mask shape a launcher might apply

	fillType is nonZero, which is what keeps the two counters open: the glyph
	contours wind in opposite directions, exactly as the type designer drew
	them, so no second shape painted in the background colour is needed.
-->
